# P12-MESH-004 solver robustness -- why the first full regression failed (logs/27a) and what the final fix is.
#
# (A) The P12-NUM-004 fallback tests' 'P12-COMP-002 breakdown' was the SAME scale-dependent false breakdown.
# A temporary diagnostic (environment-gated fprintf, removed afterwards; BiCGSTAB.cpp restored to sha 8076cd4e...)
# printed every quantity the OLD absolute test would have rejected, along the (identical up to that point) trajectory.
# The old code's breakdowns were all t . t < 1e-30 with |t|/|s| ~ 4e-8 (the pressure-correction matrix's own scale in
# that direction) and |s| ~ 1-2e-8 (the residual's): t . t is a product of two small SCALES, not an algebraic zero.
# No inner product had cancelled (none reached |dot| <= eps |x||y|).
