# (B) The first version of the fix (|(x,y)| <= eps |x||y|, no restart) failed 16 tests (logs/27a) for two reasons:
#  1. an inner product WITHOUT cancellation (e.g. one dominant term, as in advection-dominated species / alpha / k-eps
#     transport with an inlet-only shadow residual) is accurate however small it is relative to |x||y| -- the norm test
#     called it zero. Fix: compare with the rounding level of its own terms, eps * sum_i |x_i y_i| (Cauchy-Schwarz:
#     sum_i |x_i y_i| <= |x||y|, so the norm test remains a free pre-filter). With this alone (no restart), the species-
#     advection, species-conservation and alpha-advection tests passed; species coupling, turbulence channel and the two
#     fallback tests still failed (exact count not recorded -- the run output was truncated).
#  2. GENUINE rounding-level cancellation does occur mid-solve at normal scales; the old code (|dot| ~ 1e-26 > 1e-30)
#     simply continued and the recurrence recovered. Example, captured with the eps*sum|x_i y_i| build without restart
#     (SpeciesSolverCouplingTest.TransportsThroughAGenuineSIMPLESolvedPoiseuilleFlow, pressure-correction BiCGSTAB,
#     160 unknowns):
#       near-zero dot -2.234843e-26 | eps|x||y| 6.827e-26 | eps sum|xy| 3.916e-26 -> numerically zero
#       breakdown after 42 iterations, |r| 4.372e-08, b0 7.033e-03  => SIMPLE PressureCorrectionFailure
#     Fix: the standard BiCGSTAB restart (rHat = the recomputed true residual) when the residual decreased since the
#     current Krylov sequence started; otherwise Breakdown. -> all 14 non-fallback tests pass.
#  3. The two P12-NUM-004 fallback tests cannot pass with ANY scale-invariant fix: their fixture WAS the false
#     breakdown (A). They were rewritten to assert the corrected behaviour (the solve runs to its budget, the fallback
#     is never needed, results bit-identical with/without it); the fallback on a GENUINE breakdown stays covered by
#     the 13 LinearFallbackTest unit tests (a real indefinite-system breakdown and stub primaries).
